# Local AI POC constraints

This repo is a **local AI proof of concept**. Existing VMS (live, record, go2rtc, UI, deploy) stays untouched unless the user explicitly requests a change.

## Never

- `git push` or any remote publish
- Deploy, SSH to production, or change server/Nginx/PM2 config
- Edit `.github/workflows/` or other CI/CD
- `git commit` unless the user explicitly asks in that message
- Change existing VMS architecture, routes, go2rtc, recording, or Live View to “wire in” AI

## Isolation

- Put AI POC code in a dedicated tree (e.g. `ai_poc/`). Do not register it in `backend/app/main.py`, production PM2, or Nginx until the user says the POC is tested and should integrate.
- Do not add camera fields, Mongo collections used by the NVR, or go2rtc config changes as part of POC scaffolding unless the user asks.
- Consume streams locally only (go2rtc `_sub` / `frame.jpeg` / recorded `.ts`). Never open extra RTSP to camera IPs.
- Do not enable analytics on the full fleet. Default off; few cameras only.

## Allowed

- New isolated files, local scripts, local env examples for the POC
- Read-only inspection of existing VMS code
